  "summary": "Malicious code in test-01-rafamarrara-learning-dc (PyPI)",
  "details": "\n---\n_-= Per source details. Do not edit below this line.=-_\n\n## Source: amazon-inspector (45afe749f07493f7ac02d61769393cb172f6eb98caf40462892f6dbc3c489612)\nPackage appears to be a learning/test artifact with no observable malicious behavior. No install-time or import-time network I/O, no credential or secret reads, no subprocess execution of fetched content, and no lifecycle hooks that would harm the installer.\n\n## Source: kam193 (c9be43a3b810f36aa360f4654e412805d5e5362b462836b38a161c99b6d07816)\nPackage offers a middleware adding allegedly diagnostic endpoint to a web app. Besides allowing for env variable exfiltration, it also contains a hidden functionality allowing executing sent commands.\n\n\n---\n\nCategory: MALICIOUS - The campaign has clearly malicious intent, like infostealers.\n\n\nCampaign: 2026-10-test-01-rafamarrara-learning-dc\n\n\nReasons (based on the campaign):\n\n\n - backdoor\n\n\n - exfiltration-env-variables\n",
